_vrf_PLAT601_r-ndiepa_pbi_new_red_298k_red
;
PROBLEM: Unit-Cell Contains Solvent Accessible VOIDS .LE.      38 Ang**3
RESPONSE: This alert is attributed to small solvent-accessible voids 
in the structure, with a volume of approximately 38 A3. This void 
volume is comparable to that required to accommodate a single H2O 
molecule (~40 A3). However, no chemically reasonable residual electron 
density corresponding to an ordered solvent molecule could be modeled 
within the voids. The crystals were further heated at 150 °C for 20 min, 
followed by recollection of single-crystal X-ray diffraction data; 
however, voids of similar size remained. Therefore, the final model 
represents the best chemically reasonable refinement.
;

